Subject: [PATCH 11/31] fix(midea): check replies of SETTING handlers that can
 fail

Check the result byte for the SETTING commands that have a real error
path in the firmware and are used by the J15 capabilities:

- 0xC7 auto-empty duration (not 1..3 -> error)
- 0x56 dock intervals (unknown type -> error)
- 0x5C mop drying start/stop (not 0/1 -> error)
- 0x5E carpet behavior (invalid behavior -> error)

Handlers that reply OK while ignoring the input (0x51, 0x31, 0xC9
unlisted sub ids, 0x01 values 0/8, 0x63, 0x92, 0x59) are left alone, as
a check would never fire. Mop drying time (0x9B) is left to the mop
drying changes.

Based on static analysis of the handlers; untested on the robot.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaAutoEmptyDockAutoEmptyDurationControlCapabilityV2.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaAutoEmptyDockAutoEmptyDurationControlCapabilityV2.js
index 8a035b2d..141a2676 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaAutoEmptyDockAutoEmptyDurationControlCapabilityV2.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaAutoEmptyDockAutoEmptyDurationControlCapabilityV2.js
@@ -50,13 +50,17 @@ class MideaAutoEmptyDockAutoEmptyDurationControlCapabilityV2 extends AutoEmptyDo
                 throw new Error(`Received invalid duration ${newDuration}`);
         }
 
-        await this.robot.sendCommand(new MSmartPacket({
+        const response = await this.robot.sendCommand(new MSmartPacket({
             messageType: MSmartPacket.MESSAGE_TYPE.SETTING,
             payload: MSmartPacket.buildPayload(
                 MSmartConst.SETTING.SET_AUTO_EMPTY_DURATION,
                 Buffer.from([val])
             )
         }).toHexString());
+
+        if (response.payload[3] !== 0x00) {
+            throw new Error("Failed to set auto-empty duration.");
+        }
     }
 
     getProperties() {
